# =============================================================================
# EXAMPLE: Hybrid Approach (Baked Models + B2 Mount)
# =============================================================================
# Best for: Cost optimization with good performance, mixed workloads
# Cost: ~$0.50/month for 100GB on B2 + larger Docker image
# Performance: Instant for common models, medium for rare models
# Strategy: Bake frequently-used models into image, mount B2 for full library

# Storage Backend Configuration
STORAGE_BACKEND=b2-mount

# Backblaze B2 Configuration
B2_BUCKET=my-comfyui-models
B2_KEY_ID=your_key_id_here
B2_APP_KEY=your_app_key_here
B2_ENDPOINT=s3.us-west-004.backblazeb2.com
B2_REGION=us-west-004
B2_PATH=models  # Optional: subdirectory within bucket

# rclone Mount Configuration
# Smaller cache size since common models are baked into image
RCLONE_CACHE_SIZE=50G
RCLONE_CACHE_MAX_AGE=24h

# =============================================================================
# HYBRID STRATEGY OVERVIEW
# =============================================================================
# This approach combines the best of both worlds:
#
# 1. Bake frequently-used models into Docker image
#    - Top 5-10 most-used models
#    - Always available instantly
#    - No download or cache needed
#    - Increases image size by ~20-50GB
#
# 2. Mount B2 for full model library
#    - Less common models
#    - On-demand access
#    - Cost-effective storage
#    - Cached on first access
#
# 3. ComfyUI checks local first, then B2
#    - Prefers baked-in models (instant)
#    - Falls back to B2 mount (cached)
#    - Transparent to users

# =============================================================================
# IMPLEMENTATION STEPS
# =============================================================================
# 1. Identify frequently-used models
#    - Analyze usage logs
#    - Typically: 1-2 base models, 3-5 popular LoRAs
#    - Example: SD XL Base, SD 1.5, popular character LoRAs
#
# 2. Modify Dockerfile to bake models
#    Add to Dockerfile:
#    ```dockerfile
#    # Bake frequently-used models into image
#    COPY models/checkpoints/sd_xl_base_1.0.safetensors \
#         /comfyui/models/checkpoints/
#    COPY models/checkpoints/sd_v1-5-pruned.safetensors \
#         /comfyui/models/checkpoints/
#    COPY models/loras/popular_character_v1.safetensors \
#         /comfyui/models/loras/
#    ```
#
# 3. Upload full library to B2
#    ```bash
#    rclone sync ./models b2:my-comfyui-models/models --progress
#    ```
#
# 4. Configure B2 mount for remaining models
#    Use this .env configuration
#
# 5. ComfyUI will automatically use baked models first
#    - No configuration needed
#    - Falls back to B2 mount for other models

# =============================================================================
# PERFORMANCE CHARACTERISTICS
# =============================================================================
# Baked models (in Docker image):
#   - Access time: Instant (local disk)
#   - No download needed
#   - No cache needed
#   - Always available
#
# B2-mounted models (first access):
#   - Access time: 30-60 seconds (download from B2)
#   - Cached on network volume
#   - Subsequent access: Instant
#
# B2-mounted models (cached):
#   - Access time: Instant (cached)
#   - Equivalent to local disk
#   - Cache persists across restarts

# =============================================================================
# COST BREAKDOWN (100GB library, 20GB baked)
# =============================================================================
# B2 Storage: 100GB × $0.005/GB/month = $0.50/month
# B2 Egress: Minimal (only rare models downloaded)
# Network Volume: 100GB for cache + outputs = $10/month
# Docker Image: 20GB larger (no additional cost)
# Total: ~$10.50/month vs $12/month for network volume only
#
# Comparison:
#   - Network volume only (120GB): $12/month
#   - B2 mount only (100GB): $10.50/month + cache misses
#   - Hybrid (20GB baked + 80GB B2): $10.50/month + instant common models
#
# Savings: ~$1.50/month + better performance for common models

# =============================================================================
# WHEN TO USE HYBRID APPROACH
# =============================================================================
# Use hybrid when:
#   ✓ You have identifiable frequently-used models (80/20 rule)
#   ✓ You want instant access to common models
#   ✓ You want cost savings on full library
#   ✓ You can tolerate larger Docker images
#   ✓ You rebuild images periodically
#
# Don't use hybrid when:
#   ✗ Model usage is evenly distributed (no clear favorites)
#   ✗ You need to update models frequently
#   ✗ Docker image size is a concern
#   ✗ You can't rebuild images easily

# =============================================================================
# OPTIMIZATION TIPS
# =============================================================================
# 1. Analyze model usage to identify top models
#    - Check ComfyUI logs
#    - Track model access frequency
#    - Update baked models quarterly
#
# 2. Balance image size vs performance
#    - Bake 5-10 most-used models (20-50GB)
#    - Don't bake entire library (defeats purpose)
#
# 3. Update baked models periodically
#    - Rebuild image quarterly
#    - Add new popular models
#    - Remove unused models
#
# 4. Use B2_PATH to organize models
#    B2_PATH=rare-models  # Only mount rare models
#    # Baked models in image, rare models on B2
#
# 5. Monitor cache hit rate
#    - High hit rate: Hybrid working well
#    - Low hit rate: Consider baking more models
#
# 6. Consider model categories
#    - Bake: Base models, popular LoRAs
#    - B2: Experimental models, old versions, niche models

# =============================================================================
# EXAMPLE MODEL SELECTION
# =============================================================================
# Typical baked models (20-30GB total):
#   - sd_xl_base_1.0.safetensors (6.9GB)
#   - sd_xl_refiner_1.0.safetensors (6.1GB)
#   - sd_v1-5-pruned.safetensors (4.3GB)
#   - Top 5 popular LoRAs (~500MB each = 2.5GB)
#   - Essential VAE models (~1GB)
#   Total: ~20GB
#
# B2-mounted models (80GB):
#   - FLUX models (23GB each)
#   - Experimental models
#   - Old model versions
#   - Niche/specialty models
#   - Less popular LoRAs
#   Total: ~80GB

